🚨 severity: BLOCKING —
🚨 **BLOCKING: CI `crap` gate red — CRAP ratchet failed on this PR's own new code**

The `crap` quality check fails on head commit `9ddc6b33` (exit code 2), and both over-threshold functions are introduced by this PR:

```
CRAP ratchet failed: CRAP may only decrease.
NEW > 8  js/preparePRForReview.js::writeNewHunksContext: 11
NEW > 8  js/unit-tests/test_preparePRForReview.js::prGitOpsMocks: 10
0 regression(s), 2 new over threshold, 0 improvement(s), 0 removed
```
(source: `input/gh-1404/ci_failures_full.log:43838,43871-43874` — CI run 42654806484)

`writeNewHunksContext` (CC 11 at 100% coverage → CRAP 11) accumulates 6 guard clauses + try/catch + the write call in one function. Extract the early exits into small helpers, e.g.:

```javascript
function resolveNewHunksHeads(ctx, prDetails) {
    var currentHead = prDetails && prDetails.head && prDetails.head.sha;
    if (!prDetails || !prDetails.number || !currentHead) return null;
    var comments = prCommentListForRegistry(ctx.scm, prDetails.number);
    if (comments === null) return null;
    var lastHead = prNewHunks.lastReviewedHead(comments,
        { authorLogins: machineAuthorLoginsOf(ctx) });
    return prNewHunks.headsDiffer(lastHead, currentHead)
        ? { lastHead: lastHead, currentHead: currentHead } : null;
}
```
leaving `writeNewHunksContext` as resolve → diff → write, each function comfortably under the threshold. `prGitOpsMocks` (CC 10) needs the same treatment — split the gh-1404 `getDiffBetweenCommits`/`trimLargeTextForInput` mock builders out of the shared factory.

Per this PR's own new §5 rule: "a failing gate is CI breakage (🚨 BLOCKING)". All 105 new/updated unit tests pass (`run_prNewHunks.json`, `run_preparePRForReview.json`, `run_gitOps.json` — 0 failures locally), so only the ratchet refactoring is needed to green CI.

⚠️ severity: IMPORTANT —
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: comment-derived `head` is interpolated into a command string without format validation**

`fromSha`/`toSha` come from the `head` field of machine verdict-record comments, and that field is stored with no shape check — `reviewVerdicts.verdictRecordFromPayload` does `head: String(parsed.head)` with no sha-format validation. `prNewHunks.lastReviewedHead` then returns that string verbatim, and it lands here:

```javascript
var result = _runDiffCommand(cmd, 'git diff ' + fromSha + ' ' + toSha);
```

`getPRDiff` interpolates branch names from **config** (trusted input); this new function interpolates a value that was read back from **PR comment content** at review time. Anyone who can edit the machine's verdict comment (repo write access, or a compromised token writing as the bot) controls the string handed to `cli_execute_command` — the author allowlist validates *who posted* the comment, not the *payload content*, and edits don't change authorship. Defense-in-depth costs one line:

```javascript
var SHA_RE = /^[0-9a-fA-F]{7,40}$/;
if (!SHA_RE.test(String(fromSha)) || !SHA_RE.test(String(toSha))) {
    console.warn('Diff-of-diff skipped — non-sha head value in verdict record');
    return '';
}
```

Garbage input already degrades safely today (git fails → `''` → full-diff review), so this is pure hardening, not a behavior change — but an unchecked external-derived string in a shell command is exactly what the review checklist's "is external input validated?" item exists for.

